{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_gl7iqrhqye7jrzs3hn7ecmurny6t3222uexvfgvwvueve26cr2ia","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Verification complete — the translation matches the C exactly.\n\n## Result\n\n`hdr_bitrate` is the entire library (14 lines of C, one exported symbol). **No divergences found**; the Rust translation is correct, including the C's out-of-bounds table reads. Only additive changes were made (test harness + `libloading`/`libc` dev-deps + an offline cargo config); `src/lib.rs` and `c_src/` are unmodified.\n\n## Artifacts (`translation/`)\n| file | content |\n|---|---|\n| `SYMBOLS.md` | `nm -D` surface; C defines only `hdr_bitrate` + 4 CRT weak refs — all present in Rust. Symbol diff **empty**. |\n| `ERRORS.md` | 12 rows. The C has *zero* error returns/asserts/range checks, so the error surface is entirely unchecked conditions: null pointer, reserved layer (`-1` index), \"bad\" bitrate nibble (index 15), their combination, ignored bits, over-read guards, misalignment, invalid enum values. |\n| `CONFIGS.md` | 17 rows covering all `2 × 4 × 16 = 128` field combinations plus buffer-shape axes. |\n| `tests/common/mod.rs` | Loads **both** `.so`s via `libloading`; seeded xorshift PRNG. |\n| `tests/phase_b_valid.rs` | 18 tests, one per CONFIGS row. |\n| `tests/phase_c_errors.rs` | 14 tests, one per ERRORS row. |\n| `tests/phase_d_symbols.rs` | Automated `nm -D` parity assertion. |\n| `run_all_combos.sh` | Extracts features from `Cargo.toml`, sweeps power set × both profiles. |\n\n## Key findings about the C's undefined behavior\nThe C indexes `halfrate[2][3][15]` with out-of-bounds values and never validates:\n- layer bits `00` → inner index **`-1`**: with plane 0 this reads *before* the object (returns `0`); with plane 1 it **aliases `halfrate[0][2]`** (returns `0,32,48,…,256`).\n- bitrate nibble `0xF` → index **15**, past the row end; lands on element 0 of the next row (or the padding past the object) → returns `0`.\n\nI confirmed empirically against the compiled `.so` — all **65536** `(h[1], h[2])` pairs — that the Rust's zero-padded flat-table model reproduces this exactly. Guard-page tests (`PROT_NONE` neighbours) prove neither implementation reads `h[0]` or anything past `h[2]`, and a subprocess test confirms both die with the *same* `SIGSEGV` on a null pointer.\n\n## Gates\n- [x] Symbol diff empty\n- [x] All 17 CONFIGS rows pass across randomized inputs\n- [x] All 12 ERRORS rows have passing differential tests\n- [x] Binary stdout comparison **N/A** — no `add_executable` in CMake, no `[[bin]]` in Cargo.toml\n- [x] All configurations pass: `Cargo.toml` declares no `[features]`, so default and `--no-default-features` × debug/release were all run — 34/34 tests pass in each\n\nTwo notes: I added `.cargo/config.toml` with `offline = true` since the crates.io index is unreachable from this sandbox (the needed crates were already in the local cache). I also ran a negative control — injecting `0xFF` padding into the Rust table made 12 tests fail, then reverted — to confirm the harness actually detects divergence rather than passing vacuously."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":197,"cache_read_input_tokens":63210,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":197,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"fa1f8412-4b30-4936-8d08-977181c2d392","uuid":"8c519cd4-798b-4f63-b89e-0e4d6480caf8","timestamp":"2026-09-05T00:45:17.890Z"}
